#### Portal Serve Plane — `PortalHelpContext` Schema

Assembled client-side when a portal end user requests help. Grounded in the component and screen they are viewing. Never includes API response data or field values containing PHI.

```typescript
interface PortalHelpContext {
  plane: 'portal';
  persona: {
    id: string;              // role slug e.g. 'member', 'caseworker'
    displayName: string;     // e.g. 'Member', 'State Agent'
  };
  page: {
    slug: string;            // e.g. 'members', 'eligibility'
    title: string;
    messageSlots: {          // page-level content slots (title, banner, notice — NOT PHI fields)
      title?: string;
      banner?: string;
    };
  };
  component?: {              // present for component-level help
    namespace: string;       // e.g. '@member/eligibility-status'
    displayName: string;
    // AI grounding source: component.help.aiHelpContext declared in studio-manifest.json ((latest)).
    // help.fields[propName].tooltip is what renders in the UI tooltip/popover;
    // help.aiHelpContext is what the AI receives — English-only, never rendered in the UI.
    help: {
      aiHelpContext: {
        componentOverview: string;      // rich prose read by the AI; never shown to the user
        fields: {
          [propName: string]: string;   // per-field knowledge base prose for AI grounding
        };
        commonQuestions?: string[];
        limitations?: string;
      };
    };
    accessLevel: 'read-only' | 'full';  // tier-2 RBAC access level for this persona
    allowedActions: string[];            // tier-3 actions this persona can perform
  };
  locale: string;            // active portal locale (BCP-47)
  questionType: 'field' | 'page' | 'howto';
  fieldId?: string;          // propName of the field being asked about (field-level help only)
}
```

**What is NEVER included in PortalHelpContext:**
- API response data (member records, claim data, eligibility results)
- Form field values entered by the user
- PHI of any kind — SSN, DOB, member ID, claim numbers
- Session tokens or authentication data

**`help.fields` vs `help.aiHelpContext` — important distinction:**

| Attribute | `help.fields[propName].tooltip` | `help.aiHelpContext.fields[propName]` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Rendered in UI?** | Yes — tooltip/`?` popover, help panel | Never — AI grounding only |
| **Localized?** | Yes — Translation Unit via ADR-APP-005 | No — English only |
| **PHI scan?** | Standard TU pipeline | Certification gate PHI scan |
| **Purpose** | User-facing tooltip text | AI knowledge base prose |

The `aiHelpContext` block is sourced directly from `studio-manifest.json` (schema v1.0) at portal assembly time and included in the `PortalHelpContext` payload sent to the AI Gateway. It is never surfaced in the browser DOM.

**System prompt prefix (generated from context):**
```
You are a helpful assistant for a Medicaid portal. You help {persona.displayName}s
navigate the portal and complete their tasks.

The user is on the {page.title} page.
{if component: They are asking about the {component.displayName} component.
  Component overview: {component.help.aiHelpContext.componentOverview}
  {if fieldId: They are specifically asking about the "{fieldId}" field.
    Field context: {component.help.aiHelpContext.fields[fieldId] || ''}}
  This user can {component.accessLevel === 'read-only' ? 'view but not edit' : 'view and edit'} this component.
  Available actions: {component.allowedActions.join(', ') || 'none'}}

Answer in {locale}. Be helpful and simple. Do not reference technical implementation details.
Do not ask for or reference any personal health information.
```

**Schema version note:** `help.aiHelpContext` is sourced from `studio-manifest.json` schema v1.0. Domain teams must update their `mmes-common-core` dependency to the version that ships the current schema validator before `PortalHelpContext` component help can be populated. Components published against the current schema fall back to the static tooltip text (`help.fields[propName].tooltip`) without AI grounding until upgraded.

